2. ZERO THIRD-PARTY POLICY
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   epdf-org contains NO third-party code and depends on NO third-party
   libraries at runtime (open source or otherwise). This guarantees the
   Software carries no copyleft (e.g. AGPL/GPL/LGPL), attribution, or other
   obligations that would otherwise attach to a derived or combined work.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. NO DERIVATION FROM RESTRICTED SOURCES (CLEAN-ROOM)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   No part of the Software is copied, transcribed, decompiled, or line-by-line
   ported from AGPL/GPL/LGPL or any other reciprocally-licensed project. All
   behaviour is implemented independently from public technical specifications
   (ISO 32000-1/2, Unicode UAX #9/#14, OpenType, W3C HTML/CSS/SVG, PDF/A,
   PDF/UA, ICC). Test assets are self-created or public domain.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. SCOPE BOUNDARY (NO CRYPTOGRAPHY)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Cryptographic features (encryption, digital signatures, TSA/LTV/PAdES,
   ECDSA) are deliberately excluded from epdf-org. They are supplied by a
   separate build (epdf-global) or by the host application through the Service
   Provider Interfaces declared in com.epdfengine.rb.org.spi. epdf-org must
   remain crypto-free and free of any cryptographic dependency.

